[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4557020270","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-4557020270","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":4557020270,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABD56cbg","user":{"login":"solodeveloping","id":155950383,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUudLw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155950383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping","html_url":"https://github.com/solodeveloping","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T17:36:32Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T17:36:32Z","body":"For someone reading this and wanting to have more accurate primitives count, you can hide the Gizmos.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4557020270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4558234948","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-4558234948","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":4558234948,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABD7ElRA","user":{"login":"solodeveloping","id":155950383,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUudLw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155950383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping","html_url":"https://github.com/solodeveloping","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-27T20:04:56Z","updated_at":"2026-05-27T20:32:57Z","body":"(you can ignore this, just showing that good metrics is nice 😊 and performances are weird)\n\nIn another project, with another addon, primitives count increase but fps also increase, it's weird.\n\nUsually, fps increase and primitives count decrease, which I thought reflected the fact that the LOD was getting active.\n\nIt's a custom system, so maybe there is reason for that.\n\n<img width=\"725\" height=\"487\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b3899953-68d0-4c56-853e-f5b75305c0d2\" />\n\n<img width=\"806\" height=\"540\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/80164329-c48d-4029-a1d4-ffdccb811dfd\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4558234948/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5394918758","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-5394918758","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":5394918758,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABQY_tZg","user":{"login":"Arecher","id":10502115,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTAyMTE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10502115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher","html_url":"https://github.com/Arecher","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arecher/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-24T12:04:36Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T12:41:55Z","body":"The **fact that Godot specific elements, such as gizmos add to the primitive count is very unintuitive**. I'd expect the statistics to be representative of what would be shown in an **exported build**, so it can be used for debugging. Right now, the primitive count doesn't give a usable number, because it's near impossible to determine how bloated the number is by Godot additions and therefore impossible to get a *true* scene primitive value.\n\nAt the very least it should split the values, so it shows the amount of primitives the meshes and nodes in the scene add AND the amount that Godot itself added for editor components.\n\n```Primitives: 1000 (+600 editor)``` or something along those lines.\n\nThat way you can actually look at a scene with a single mesh, and use the primitive statistic to compare it to your 3D model software statistics (keeping the 2x to 3x higher number in mind) or do proper evaluations as to whether the mesh has an excess amount of triangles.\n\nHowever, perhaps apart from EditorPlugins, I cannot think of a single scenario where someone would need to see the amount of primitives added by native gizmos and other elements, so perhaps just excluding them by default (perhaps with an option to reenable them with editor settings) would be better.\n\nAn additional `MESH_PRIMITIVES` statistic, which would show the amount of primitives for the **selected object**, disregarding any culling or additional passes (so just a simple triangle count) would also be extremely helpful to have (https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/248). Getting an accurate count somewhere would help confirm exporting issues (such as degenerate geometry or duplicate faces). This could be shown in the Editor window, but perhaps the (import) inspector would be even better. As long as that information is accessible somewhere.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5394918758/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5741650731","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-5741650731","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":5741650731,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVjqjKw","user":{"login":"solodeveloping","id":155950383,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUudLw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155950383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping","html_url":"https://github.com/solodeveloping","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-19T11:56:31Z","updated_at":"2026-09-19T11:56:31Z","body":"> However, perhaps apart from EditorPlugins, I cannot think of a single scenario where someone would need to see the amount of primitives added by native gizmos and other elements\n\nYou want it to detect where FPS drop come from, you can get -100FPS if you have some things enabled (grid and collider shape debugging for instance).\n\nI have updated one of the addons that was reporting individual MeshInstanced3D counts so that it would report the children too but I haven't pushed a MR.\n\nI eventually wanted to make a tool that would report it like it's done for hard drive space (treemap/pie chart), but I identified the problem and it's time consuming to make 🤷‍♂️ \n\n> disregarding any culling\n\nI think it's something you want (maybe you meant LOD too). Having as most information as possible would be really nice.\n\nIt's out of the scope but identifying which material / object is dropping the FPS the most would be nice (it's doable as an addon, you have to do the same thing you would do manually: hide/remove the objects, see how it impacts the FPS)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5741650731/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5943383774","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-5943383774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":5943383774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYkDW3g","user":{"login":"Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou","html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T00:38:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T00:41:37Z","body":"Implementing https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15416 should help clarify the source of draw calls/primitives/objects, although it doesn't work consistently for all light types yet. Aside of that, there's also the depth prepass in Forward+, which can significantly increase the reported statistics.\n\nExcluding gizmos from the reported statistics is unfortunately difficult without having to introduce low-level engine changes ([which we'd prefer avoiding for editor-only features](https://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/development/engine/best_practices.html#prefer-local-solutions)). The only other way to do so at a \"local\" scope is to manually count how many draw calls, objects and primitives gizmos are drawing, and subtract these from the reported counts.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5943383774/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5945182102","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-5945182102","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":5945182102,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYlxHlg","user":{"login":"solodeveloping","id":155950383,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUudLw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155950383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping","html_url":"https://github.com/solodeveloping","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T03:40:55Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T03:40:55Z","body":"I think that nothing should be removed by default (to understand where a FPS drop comes from in the editor for instance)\n\nSubstracting is nice\n\nCan we modify the Editor FPS layout? I think we can't no? As an addon (I'm not 100% sure)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5945182102/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5951899147","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-5951899147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":5951899147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYsLGCw","user":{"login":"solodeveloping","id":155950383,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUudLw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155950383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping","html_url":"https://github.com/solodeveloping","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T12:02:03Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T12:02:10Z","body":"The grid really eats a lot of FPS (400 on a project I just tested, it went from 500 to 100)\n\nThere must be something \"wrong\" (no offense, let's improve it) with how it's implemented, I can't explain it (I wish I could inspect it to help with the improvement 🤷‍♂️)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5951899147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5951908675","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-5951908675","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":5951908675,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYsLrQw","user":{"login":"solodeveloping","id":155950383,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUudLw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155950383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping","html_url":"https://github.com/solodeveloping","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T12:02:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T12:02:51Z","body":"I wish we would see the fragment invocation calls (I guess this is outside the scope of this issue), because it can matter a lot","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5951908675/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5952153757","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119825#issuecomment-5952153757","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119825","id":5952153757,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYsaonQ","user":{"login":"solodeveloping","id":155950383,"node_id":"U_kgDOCUudLw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/155950383?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping","html_url":"https://github.com/solodeveloping","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/solodeveloping/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-02T12:17:47Z","updated_at":"2026-10-02T12:17:47Z","body":"How reliable are the FPS anyway?\n\nI thought I was passing to a new render size, 512 to 1024 maybe, but the last one was reliably switching to 400, then reliably stayed at 80, and now it's back at 400 (and I'm just playing with the viewport size, moving the docks around)\n\n<img width=\"1118\" height=\"498\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/65a4bf47-51a9-442d-8397-d677eed440de\" />\n\n<img width=\"1119\" height=\"511\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cc900c3b-a71d-4352-b522-fab39dab9b77\" />\n\n<img width=\"1508\" height=\"540\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8ab3c8f4-7af6-4200-a88f-91a2e708faf6\" />\n\nI moved it again and it went back to 90\n\n<img width=\"1513\" height=\"540\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1babce5c-0e33-453e-9bfc-fc6f44861d67\" />\n\nThe 512 definitively plays here, at 512 or 513 it was at 80, did not matter what size it was, and right after I went below, it went to 400\n\n<img width=\"1507\" height=\"504\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4da51195-c611-440e-905a-8b4c25a35a08\" />\n\nIf I had to guess, the fragment something (not sure who has this role) draw on 1024 and not the exact value?\n\nBut now I'm back at \"full\" screen and it's 300, I don't get it\n\n<img width=\"1512\" height=\"539\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19788fad-2db4-4dc3-a026-44fd39af50a1\" />\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5952153757/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]